rationale:
`requirements.sdk.habeas.github_nodes.related` has no `{test}` references or `:test:` anchors, so no test covers it. The obligations are:
- the FIXME review uses an agent criterion to judge whether each linked issue's title and opening post describe the FIXME's gap;
- the criterion selects the FIXME's tracking-issue edges through the SDK's tracked interface;
- the criterion supplies the FIXME and selected issue contents through tracked reads or ask insertions;
- a completed "unrelated" assessment fails that issue's relevance check.

I searched `src` for relevance or unrelated-answer tests. None cover this requirement. The "unrelated" matches in `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]` and elsewhere are fixture names, not tests of this behavior.

A `{fixme}` on `requirements.sdk.habeas.github_nodes.related` in `src/sdk.rs#enum[HabeasNode]` acknowledges the gap. It cites `nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem#26`, which is open. Its body says the agent-based relevance criterion is deferred and that tests do not yet check tracking-edge selection, delivered FIXME/issue snapshots, or unrelated answers. That matches the missing-test gap I found, and nothing I reviewed shows the gap has been closed.
